When C code such as the signal dispatch called an object whose __call__
metamethod is a C function, the VM ran the interpreter after the call as
if a closure had been called, which continued the bytecode frame on top
of the stack from the wrong position and corrupted the memory.

-- Testcase --
{%
	signal("SIGUSR1", proto({}, { __call__: print }));
	system("kill -USR1 $PPID");
	print("\nafter\n");
%}
-- End --

-- Expect stdout --
10
after
-- End --
